    // Aliases & CSRF & Preventing
    'Bypassing rate limiting using aliases' => 'Melewati pembatasan laju memakai alias',
    "Ordinarily, GraphQL objects can't contain multiple properties with the same name. Aliases enable you to bypass this restriction by explicitly naming the properties you want the API to return. You can use aliases to return multiple instances of the same type of object in one request." => 'Alias GraphQL memampukan penggabungan beberapa pemanggilan objek atau mutasi yang sama dalam satu permintaan HTTP dengan memberi nama hasil yang berbeda.',
    'For more information on GraphQL aliases, see [[A0]]Aliases[[/A0]].' => 'Untuk penjelasan sintaksnya, lihat bagian [[A0]]Alias[[/A0]].',
    'While aliases are intended to limit the number of API calls you need to make, they can also be used to brute force a GraphQL endpoint.' => 'Selain mengurangi jumlah panggilan jaringan, alias sering disalahgunakan untuk serangan brute-force.',
    'Many endpoints will have some sort of rate limiter in place to prevent brute force attacks. Some rate limiters work based on the number of HTTP requests received rather than the number of operations performed on the endpoint. Because aliases effectively enable you to send multiple queries in a single HTTP message, they can bypass this restriction.' => 'Karena banyak rate limiter hanya menghitung jumlah permintaan HTTP alih-alih jumlah operasi di dalamnya, mengirim ratusan alias dalam satu permintaan HTTP dapat melewati batas laju tersebut.',
    'The simplified example below shows a series of aliased queries checking whether store discount codes are valid. This operation could potentially bypass rate limiting as it is a single HTTP request, even though it could potentially be used to check a vast number of discount codes at once.' => 'Contoh berikut menguji beberapa kode promo sekaligus dalam satu permintaan HTTP menggunakan alias:',
    'GraphQL CSRF' => 'CSRF pada GraphQL',
    'Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerabilities enable an attacker to induce users to perform actions that they do not intend to perform. This is done by creating a malicious website that forges a cross-domain request to the vulnerable application.' => 'Kerentanan cross-site request forgery (CSRF) memampukan penyerang memaksa peramban korban mengirim aksi tanpa sepengetahuannya melalui situs web berbahaya.',
    'For more information on CSRF vulnerabilities in general, see the [[A0]]CSRF academy topic[[/A0]].' => 'Untuk pemahaman umum mengenai CSRF, baca [[A0]]topik materi CSRF[[/A0]].',
    "GraphQL can be used as a vector for CSRF attacks, whereby an attacker creates an exploit that causes a victim's browser to send a malicious query as the victim user." => 'GraphQL dapat menjadi sarana CSRF apabila peramban korban dipaksa mengirim kueri atau mutasi berbahaya atas nama sesi korban.',
    'How do CSRF over GraphQL vulnerabilities arise?' => 'Bagaimana CSRF pada GraphQL muncul?',
    'CSRF vulnerabilities can arise where a GraphQL endpoint does not validate the content type of the requests sent to it and no CSRF tokens are implemented.' => 'Celah CSRF pada GraphQL muncul ketika endpoint tidak memvalidasi Content-Type secara ketat serta tidak mewajibkan token anti-CSRF.',
    "POST requests that use a content type of [[C0]] are secure against forgery as long as the content type is validated. In this case, an attacker wouldn't be able to make the victim's browser send this request even if the victim were to visit a malicious site." => 'Permintaan POST bertipe [[C0]] aman terhadap formulir HTML standar selama server menolak Content-Type selain tipe tersebut.',
    'However, alternative methods such as GET, or any request that has a content type of [[C0]], can be sent by a browser and so may leave users vulnerable to attack if the endpoint accepts these requests. Where this is the case, attackers may be able to craft exploits to send malicious requests to the API.' => 'Namun jika endpoint tetap menerima GET atau POST bertipe [[C0]], situs pihak ketiga dapat memicu permintaan lintas situs dari peramban korban dengan mudah.',
    'The steps to construct a CSRF attack and deliver an exploit are the same for GraphQL-based CSRF vulnerabilities as they are for "regular" CSRF vulnerabilities. For more information on this process, see [[A0]]How to construct a CSRF attack[[/A0]].' => 'Tahapan pembuatan eksploitnya identik dengan CSRF biasa; pelajari detailnya pada [[A0]]Cara menyusun serangan CSRF[[/A0]].',
    'Preventing GraphQL attacks' => 'Mencegah serangan GraphQL',
    'To prevent many common GraphQL attacks, take the following steps when you deploy your API to production:' => 'Terapkan langkah-langkah berikut sebelum merilis layanan GraphQL ke lingkungan produksi:',
    'If your API is not intended for use by the general public, disable introspection on it. This makes it harder for an attacker to gain information about how the API works, and reduces the risk of unwanted information disclosure.' => 'Matikan fitur introspection apabila API tidak ditujukan bagi pengembang publik guna mempersulit pemetaan skema.',
    'For information on how to disable introspection in the Apollo GraphQL platform, see [[A0]]this blog post[[/A0]].' => 'Panduan menonaktifkan introspection di Apollo tersedia pada [[A0]]artikel berikut[[/A0]].',
    "If your API is intended for use by the general public then you will likely need to leave introspection enabled. However, you should review the API's schema to make sure that it does not expose unintended fields to the public." => 'Jika API memang terbuka untuk publik dan introspection tetap aktif, tinjau ulang seluruh skema agar tidak ada field privat yang terekspos.',
    'Make sure that suggestions are disabled. This prevents attackers from being able to use Clairvoyance or similar tools to glean information about the underlying schema.' => 'Matikan fitur suggestions agar alat seperti Clairvoyance tidak bisa menebak nama field dari pesan error.',
    "Make sure that your API's schema does not expose any private user fields, such as email addresses or user IDs." => 'Pastikan skema maupun resolver menerapkan kontrol otorisasi ketat untuk setiap field sensitif pengguna.',
    'Preventing GraphQL brute force attacks' => 'Mencegah serangan brute force GraphQL',
    'It is sometimes possible to bypass standard rate limiting when using GraphQL APIs. For an example of this, see the [[A0]]Bypassing rate limiting using aliases[[/A0]] section.' => 'Pembatasan berbasis jumlah permintaan HTTP bisa ditembus menggunakan alias seperti dijelaskan pada bagian [[A0]]Melewati pembatasan laju memakai alias[[/A0]].',
    'With this in mind, there are design steps that you can take to defend your API against brute force attacks. This generally involves restricting the complexity of queries accepted by the API, and reducing the opportunity for attackers to execute denial-of-service (DoS) attacks.' => 'Untuk menahannya sekaligus mencegah serangan DoS, batasi kompleksitas setiap kueri yang boleh dieksekusi server.',
    'To defend against brute force attacks:' => 'Praktik mitigasi yang disarankan meliputi:',
    'Limit the query depth of your API\'s queries. The term "query depth" refers to the number of levels of nesting within a query. Heavily-nested queries can have significant performance implications, and can potentially provide an opportunity for DoS attacks if they are accepted. By limiting the query depth your API accepts, you can reduce the chances of this happening.' => 'Batasi kedalaman bersarang kueri (query depth) agar kueri berulang yang dalam tidak membebani server.',
    'Configure operation limits. Operation limits enable you to configure the maximum number of unique fields, aliases, and root fields that your API can accept.' => 'Tetapkan batas jumlah maksimum alias, field root, maupun field unik dalam satu permintaan.',
    'Configure the maximum amount of bytes a query can contain.' => 'Batasi ukuran byte maksimum isi kueri yang diterima server.',
    'Consider implementing cost analysis on your API. Cost analysis is a process whereby a library application identifies the resource cost associated with running queries as they are received. If a query would be too computationally complex to run, the API drops it.' => 'Terapkan analisis beban kueri (cost analysis) untuk menolak permintaan yang membutuhkan sumber daya komputasi terlalu besar.',
    'For information on how to implement these features in Apollo, see [[A0]]this blog post[[/A0]].' => 'Informasi penerapan pembatasan di Apollo dapat dibaca pada [[A0]]artikel berikut[[/A0]].',
    'Preventing CSRF over GraphQL' => 'Mencegah CSRF pada GraphQL',
    'To defend against GraphQL CSRF vulnerabilities specifically, make sure of the following when designing your API:' => 'Khusus untuk mencegah CSRF pada GraphQL, pastikan hal berikut:',
    'Your API only accepts queries over JSON-encoded POST.' => 'Endpoint hanya menerima permintaan POST berformat JSON.',
    'The API validates that content provided matches the supplied content type.' => 'Server memverifikasi kesesuaian isi payload dengan header Content-Type yang dikirim.',
    'The API has a secure CSRF token mechanism.' => 'Terapkan mekanisme token CSRF atau pemeriksaan header kustom yang aman.',

    // What is GraphQL page
    'GraphQL is an API query language that is designed to facilitate efficient communication between clients and servers. It enables the user to specify exactly what data they want in the response, helping to avoid the large response objects and multiple calls that can sometimes be seen with REST APIs.' => 'GraphQL adalah bahasa kueri API yang memudahkan klien menentukan secara persis field data apa yang ingin diterima, sehingga mencegah pengambilan data berlebih maupun panggilan berulang seperti pada REST API tradisional.',
    "GraphQL services define a contract through which a client can communicate with a server. The client doesn't need to know where the data resides. Instead, clients send queries to a GraphQL server, which fetches data from the relevant places. As GraphQL is platform-agnostic, it can be implemented with a wide range of programming languages and can be used to communicate with virtually any data store." => 'Layanan GraphQL mendefinisikan skema kontrak antarklien dan server tanpa klien perlu tahu letak sumber data sebenarnya di balik layar.',
    'This page offers an overview of what GraphQL is and how it works. For specific information on how to test for GraphQL vulnerabilities, see [[A0]]GraphQL API vulnerabilities[[/A0]].' => 'Halaman ini merangkum cara kerja dasar GraphQL. Untuk teknik audit keamanannya, lihat [[A0]]Kerentanan API GraphQL[[/A0]].',
    'How GraphQL works' => 'Cara kerja GraphQL',
    "GraphQL schemas define the structure of the service's data, listing the available objects (known as types), fields, and relationships." => 'Skema GraphQL menjabarkan struktur data layanan beserta seluruh tipe objek, field, dan relasinya.',
    'The data described by a GraphQL schema can be manipulated using three types of operation:' => 'Data di dalam skema GraphQL berinteraksi melalui tiga jenis operasi:',
    'Queries fetch data.' => 'Query untuk membaca atau mengambil data.',
    'Mutations add, change, or remove data.' => 'Mutation untuk menambah, mengubah, atau menghapus data.',
    'Subscriptions are similar to queries, but set up a permanent connection by which a server can proactively push data to a client in the specified format.' => 'Subscription untuk membangun koneksi persisten agar server dapat mendorong pembaruan data secara real-time ke klien.',
    'All GraphQL operations use the same endpoint, and are generally sent as a POST request. This is significantly different to REST APIs, which use operation-specific endpoints across a range of HTTP methods. With GraphQL, the type and name of the operation define how the query is handled, rather than the endpoint it is sent to or the HTTP method used.' => 'Berbeda dari REST yang memisah URL per resource, seluruh operasi GraphQL umumnya dikirim lewat POST ke satu endpoint yang sama.',
    'GraphQL services generally respond to operations with a JSON object in the structure requested.' => 'Server GraphQL membalas operasi tersebut dengan objek JSON yang bentuknya mengikuti struktur permintaan klien.',
    'What is a GraphQL schema?' => 'Apa itu skema GraphQL?',
    'In GraphQL, the schema represents a contract between the frontend and backend of the service. It defines the data available as a series of types, using a human-readable schema definition language. These types can then be implemented by a service.' => 'Skema merupakan kontrak antara frontend dan backend yang ditulis memakai Schema Definition Language agar mudah dibaca.',
    'Most of the types defined are object types, which define the objects available and the fields and arguments they have. Each field has its own type, which can either be another object or a scalar, enum, union, interface, or custom type.' => 'Sebagian besar definisi berupa object type beserta field dan argumen yang bisa bertipe skalar, enum, objek lain, atau tipe khusus.',
    'The example below shows a simple schema definition for a Product type. The [[C0]] operator indicates that the field is non-nullable when called (that is, mandatory).' => 'Contoh skema Product di bawah ini memakai tanda [[C0]] untuk menandakan field wajib tidak boleh bernilai null:',
    'Schemas must also include at least one available query. Usually, they also contain details of available mutations.' => 'Skema wajib mendefinisikan minimal satu query serta lazimnya menyertakan daftar mutation yang didukung.',
    'What are GraphQL queries?' => 'Apa itu query GraphQL?',
    'GraphQL queries retrieve data from the data store. They are roughly equivalent to GET requests in a REST API.' => 'Query bertugas mengambil data dari server, sepadan dengan permintaan GET pada REST API.',
    'Queries usually have the following key components:' => 'Sebuah query biasanya memuat komponen utama berikut:',
    'A [[C0]] operation type. This is technically optional but encouraged, as it explicitly tells the server that the incoming request is a query.' => 'Tipe operasi [[C0]] sebagai penanda eksplisit kepada server.',
    'A query name. This can be anything you want. The query name is optional, but encouraged as it can help with debugging.' => 'Nama operasi kueri (opsional, namun sangat membantu saat debugging).',
    'A data structure. This is the data that the query should return.' => 'Daftar struktur field data yang ingin dikembalikan dalam respons.',
    'Optionally, one or more arguments. These are used to create queries that return details of a specific object (for example "give me the name and description of the product that has the ID 123").' => 'Argumen opsional untuk menyaring objek tertentu, misalnya mengambil produk ber-ID 123.',
    'The example below shows a query called [[C0]] that requests the name, and description fields of a product with the [[C1]] of [[C2]].' => 'Contoh kueri [[C0]] berikut meminta nama dan deskripsi produk dengan [[C1]] bernilai [[C2]]:',
    'Note that the product type may contain more fields in the schema than those requested here. The ability to request only the data you need is a significant part of the flexibility of GraphQL.' => 'Meski tipe Product punya lebih banyak field di server, klien hanya menerima field yang benar-benar diminta.',
    'What are GraphQL mutations?' => 'Apa itu mutation GraphQL?',
    'Mutations change data in some way, either adding, deleting, or editing it. They are roughly equivalent to a REST API\'s POST, PUT, and DELETE methods.' => 'Mutation berfungsi memodifikasi data (tambah, ubah, hapus), mirip metode POST, PUT, dan DELETE pada REST API.',
    'Like queries, mutations have an operation type, name, and structure for the returned data. However, mutations always take an input of some type. This can be an inline value, but in practice is generally provided as a variable.' => 'Strukturnya mirip query, tetapi mutation selalu menerima masukan data baik secara langsung maupun melalui variabel.',
    'The example below shows a mutation to create a new product and its associated response. In this case, the service is configured to automatically assign an ID to new products, which has been returned as requested.' => 'Contoh mutation pembuatan produk baru beserta respons JSON yang mengembalikan ID otomatis:',
    'Components of queries and mutations' => 'Komponen pada query dan mutation',
    'The GraphQL syntax includes several common components for queries and mutations.' => 'Sintaks query dan mutation berbagi beberapa elemen dasar berikut.',
    'Fields' => 'Fields',
    'All GraphQL types contain items of queryable data called fields. When you send a query or mutation, you specify which of the fields you want the API to return. The response mirrors the content specified in the request.' => 'Setiap tipe di GraphQL tersusun dari satuan data bernama field. Struktur JSON respons mencerminkan field apa saja yang diminta di kueri.',
    'The example below shows a query to get ID and name details for all employees, and its associated response. In this case, [[C0]], [[C1]], and [[C2]] are the fields requested.' => 'Contoh berikut mengambil detail karyawan untuk field [[C0]], [[C1]], dan [[C2]]:',
    'Arguments' => 'Argumen',
    'Arguments are values that are provided for specific fields. The arguments that can be accepted for a type are defined in the schema.' => 'Argumen adalah nilai parameter yang diberikan kepada field tertentu sesuai definisi skema.',
    'When you send a query or mutation that contains arguments, the GraphQL server determines how to respond based on its configuration. For example, it might return a specific object rather than details of all objects.' => 'Server menggunakan argumen tersebut untuk memfilter atau mencari data spesifik, alih-alih mengembalikan seluruh koleksi.',
    'The example below shows a [[C0]] request that takes an employee ID as an argument. In this case, the server responds with only the details of the employee who matches that ID.' => 'Contoh [[C0]] berikut menerima argumen ID agar server hanya mengembalikan data karyawan yang sesuai:',
    'If user-supplied arguments are used to access objects directly then a GraphQL API can be vulnerable to access control vulnerabilities such as insecure direct object references (IDOR).' => 'Bila argumen pengguna langsung mengambil data tanpa pemeriksaan hak akses, endpoint rentan terhadap IDOR.',
    'Variables' => 'Variabel',
    'Variables enable you to pass dynamic arguments, rather than having arguments directly within the query itself.' => 'Variabel memampukan pengiriman nilai argumen secara dinamis terpisah dari teks kueri utama.',
    'Variable-based queries use the same structure as queries using inline arguments, but certain aspects of the query are taken from a separate JSON-based variables dictionary. They enable you to reuse a common structure among multiple queries, with only the value of the variable itself changing.' => 'Dengan menaruh nilai dinamis pada objek JSON variabel terpisah, struktur kueri dapat dipakai ulang berulang kali.',
    'When building a query or mutation that uses variables, you need to:' => 'Saat memakai variabel dalam GraphQL, lakukan tiga langkah ini:',
    'Declare the variable and type.' => 'Deklarasikan nama variabel beserta tipe datanya pada tajuk operasi.',
    'Add the variable name in the appropriate place in the query.' => 'Gunakan nama variabel tersebut sebagai nilai argumen di dalam kueri.',
    'Pass the variable key and value from the variable dictionary.' => 'Kirimkan pasangan kunci dan nilai variabel pada objek JSON terpisah.',
    'The example below shows the same query as in the previous example, but with the ID passed as a variable instead of as a direct part of the query string.' => 'Contoh berikut memperlihatkan pemindahan argumen ID ke dalam kamus variabel:',
    'In this example, the variable is declared in the first line with ([[C0]]). The [[C1]] indicates that this is a required field for this query. It is then used as an argument in the second line with ([[C2]]). Finally, the value of the variable itself is set in the variable JSON dictionary. For information on how to test for these vulnerabilities, see [[A0]]GraphQL API vulnerabilities[[/A0]].' => 'Variabel dideklarasikan pada baris pertama dengan ([[C0]]) di mana [[C1]] menandakan wajib diisi, lalu dirujuk dengan ([[C2]]). Baca juga [[A0]]Kerentanan API GraphQL[[/A0]].',
    'Aliases' => 'Alias',
    "GraphQL objects can't contain multiple properties with the same name. For example, the following query is invalid because it tries to return the [[C0]] type twice." => 'Objek GraphQL tidak boleh mengembalikan dua properti bernama sama sehingga kueri yang meminta [[C0]] dua kali tanpa alias akan ditolak:',
    'Aliases enable you to bypass this restriction by explicitly naming the properties you want the API to return. You can use aliases to return multiple instances of the same type of object in one request. This helps to reduce the number of API calls needed.' => 'Alias mengatasi batas itu dengan memberi nama unik pada setiap hasil pemanggilan dalam satu kueri.',
    'In the example below, the query uses aliases to specify a unique name for both products. This query now passes validation, and the details are returned.' => 'Pada contoh ini, kedua pemanggilan produk diberi alias unik sehingga kueri lolos validasi:',
    'Using aliases with mutations effectively enables you to send multiple GraphQL messages in one HTTP request.' => 'Penggunaan alias pada mutation memampukan eksekusi beberapa aksi sekaligus dalam satu permintaan HTTP.',
    'For more information on how to use this technique to bypass some rate limit controls, see [[A0]]Bypassing rate limiting using aliases[[/A0]].' => 'Pelajari teknik penyalahgunaannya di [[A0]]Melewati pembatasan laju memakai alias[[/A0]].',
    'Fragments' => 'Fragments',
    'Fragments are reusable parts of queries or mutations. They contain a subset of the fields belonging to the associated type.' => 'Fragment adalah kumpulan field dari suatu tipe yang dapat dipakai ulang di berbagai query atau mutation.',
    'Once defined, they can be included in queries or mutations. If they are subsequently changed, the change is included in every query or mutation that calls the fragment.' => 'Setiap perubahan pada definisi fragment otomatis berlaku di seluruh operasi yang memanggilnya.',
    'The example below shows a [[C0]] query in which the details of the product are contained in a [[C1]] fragment.' => 'Contoh berikut menaruh detail produk di dalam fragment [[C1]] lalu menyisipkannya ke kueri [[C0]]:',
    'Subscriptions' => 'Subscriptions',
    'Subscriptions are a special type of query. They enable clients to establish a long-lived connection with a server so that the server can then push real-time updates to the client without the need to continually poll for data. They are primarily useful for small changes to large objects and for functionality that requires small real-time updates (like chat systems or collaborative editing).' => 'Subscription adalah operasi khusus untuk membuka koneksi jangka panjang agar server dapat mengirim pembaruan real-time seperti fitur obrolan atau kolaborasi langsung.',
    'As with regular queries and mutations, the subscription request defines the shape of the data to be returned.' => 'Sama seperti query, klien menentukan bentuk field yang ingin diterima melalui subscription.',
    'Subscriptions are commonly implemented using WebSockets.' => 'Subscription umumnya diimplementasikan di atas protokol WebSockets.',
    'Introspection' => 'Introspection',
    'Introspection is a built-in GraphQL function that enables you to query a server for information about the schema. It is commonly used by applications such as GraphQL IDEs and documentation generation tools.' => 'Introspection memungkinkan klien menanyakan seluruh struktur skema dari server, dan lazim dipakai oleh IDE atau pembangkit dokumentasi otomatis.',
    'Like regular queries, you can specify the fields and structure of the response you want to be returned. For example, you might want the response to only contain the names of available mutations.' => 'Klien bebas memilih detail yang diinginkan, misalnya hanya meminta daftar nama mutation.',
    'Introspection can represent a serious information disclosure risk, as it can be used to access potentially sensitive information (such as field descriptions) and help an attacker to learn how they can interact with the API. It is best practice for introspection to be disabled in production environments.' => 'Karena berisiko membocorkan struktur API dan deskripsi field sensitif, introspection sebaiknya dimatikan di lingkungan produksi.',
    'For more information on how to use GraphQL introspection queries and test for introspection vulnerabilities, see [[A0]]GraphQL API vulnerabilities[[/A0]].' => 'Pelajari teknik pengujiannya lebih lanjut pada materi [[A0]]Kerentanan API GraphQL[[/A0]].',
];
